{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Polyrith"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.exists_unit_circle_disc_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.exists_unit_circle_disc_zero","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L159-L168","doc":"**The refutation.** There is a point of the unit circle at which the GGM\ncurve's discriminant vanishes — so two of its three `y`-branches collide there,\nand `min |disc| = 0` on `|x| = 1`, not `0.348`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:fivetwo-discriminant-vanishes","label":"prop:fivetwo-discriminant-vanishes","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/fivetwo-discriminant-vanishes.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.onCircle_add_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.onCircle_add_inv","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L144-L157","doc":"`x + 1/x = u` at the circle point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.onCircle_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.onCircle_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L138-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.norm_onCircle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.norm_onCircle","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L131-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.normSq_onCircle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.normSq_onCircle","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L124-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.onCircle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.onCircle","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L121-L122","doc":"The unit-circle point with `x + 1/x = u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.exists_root_Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.exists_root_Q","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L107-L114","doc":"**`Q` has a real root in `(−2,−1)`.** This is the whole refutation: `(−2,−1)`\nsits inside `[−2,2]`, which is exactly the range of `x + 1/x` on `|x| = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q_continuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q_continuous","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L104-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Qc_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Qc_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L95-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc_eq_Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc_eq_Q","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L89-L93","doc":"**The palindromic reduction.** `disc x = x⁴ · Q(x + 1/x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Q","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L86-L87","doc":"…and over `ℝ`, where the sign change lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Qc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.Qc","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L83-L84","doc":"The palindromic reduction, over `ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.ggm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.ggm_one","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc_one","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L78-L79","doc":"At `x = 1` the curve is the 5₂ polynomial and the discriminant is `−23`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc_eq_cubic_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc_eq_cubic_formula","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L67-L76","doc":"`disc` really is the standard cubic discriminant\n`18abcd − 4b³d + b²c² − 4ac³ − 27a²d²` of `ggm`, whose coefficients are\n`a = x`, `b = −(x²+1)`, `c = x²+x+1`, `d = −x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.disc","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L63-L65","doc":"`disc_y` of `ggm`, expanded. Palindromic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.ggm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDiscriminant.ggm","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoDiscriminant.lean#L59-L61","doc":"The GGM deformed 5₂ curve as a cubic in `y`: at `x = 1` it is the 5₂\npolynomial `y³ − 2y² + 3y − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}